Z||000000||G25C||07-29-99||07:55 AM||||<br>I talked to a fiero owner at the gas station the other day, and as we talked he said that one modification he wants to do is mount a small fan under the 2 side vents on either side of the rear deck that let out hot air from the engine compartment.<p>Would this realy be nessacery?  Would it actually help much.  Ive never thought about doing it myself.<p>Is was a 85 coupe and he said he didnt have the internal fan thats in the rear trunk side like my  87 GT does.
Z||000001||vurbanson||07-29-99||03:06 PM||||Hey<p>I have an 87 GT.  I have the extra fan in the rear side also.  No, I don't think it's necessary to install extra fans in the vents.  You will notice that the extra factory fan is there to blow cold air onto the alternator and coil, not to extract hot air from the compartment.  The car shouldn't run hot all the time, and if it does, there's a problem.  I run my car on the 165 degree thermostat and the temperature very, very rarely climbs over a quarter, and when it does, the front fan is more than adequate.
Z||000002||G25C||07-29-99||09:54 PM||||I never have a problem with my GT getting hot either, it always stays low and if it does climb a little the fan takes over and cools it down.  I didnt think it would be neccassary for the extra fans, but i was curious none the less.<p>thanks for the reply
