Z||000010||G25C||07-31-99||08:42 AM||||Im not sure.  When i bought my Fiero, my buddies and i had stared at the tubes trying to figure out what they were for and where they came from.  I didnt even know there was a fan in my side trunk compartment.  Ive never noticed air coming out, but thats when the car is not in motion.   Mabey it only works going down the road or if you motor gets to a certain tempature like the front cooling fan does.<p>The air that does come out, whether hot or whatever, i guess is directed at certain equipment on the motor and (i guess) moves the air around the engine compartment to help in circulating it out.<p>Kinda like when your in the factory and its extremely hot and you have a fan on you but its just blowing hot air cause its so hot in the building.  It not cold air blowing on you, but at least its air moving and pushing air around you.<p>Im just taking a wild stab at this...i have never talked to anyone about this rear fan and tube assembly.  If someone knows more about this please reply.
Z||000011||Phil||07-31-99||11:13 AM||||The engine compartment fan was discussed in an earlier thread. The fan is not on the later models (V6) The fan comes on with the rad. fan and blows outside air on the coil and alt.
